---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_URL, FEEDBACK_FORM_URL, INTEREST_LIST_URL, beamcashFlow } from "../content/site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="BeamCash Demo - SkanPay"
  description="BeamCash is the SkanPay product proof for QR payment requests, buyer review, and seller-readable checkout status."
  activePath="/beamcash-demo/"
>
  <section class="app-product-hero">
    <div class="app-hero-inner">
      <div class="app-hero-copy">
        <div class="app-logo-block square-logo-block">
          <img class="beamcash-brand-icon" src="/beamcash/beamcash-logo-mark.svg" alt="BeamCash logo" />
        </div>
        <p class="page-label">BeamCash by SkanPay</p>
        <h1>QR checkout for quick in-person payments.</h1>
        <p class="lead-copy">
          BeamCash shows the core payment handoff: a seller displays a QR request, the buyer reviews the recipient and amount, and the seller gets a clear result.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-proof">
          <span>Seller QR</span>
          <span>Buyer review</span>
          <span>Status result</span>
        </div>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button primary" href="#walkthrough">See the flow</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={FEEDBACK_FORM_URL}>Give feedback</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="app-screen-hero" aria-label="BeamCash app screens">
        <div class="demo-hero-frame">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-app-seller-dashboard.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard with Scan to Pay QR code" />
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-app-buyer-checkout.png" alt="BeamCash checkout screen with merchant profile and payment amount options" />
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section demo-purpose">
    <div class="section-inner demo-purpose-inner">
      <div>
        <span>Why BeamCash exists</span>
        <h2>A product proof for the SkanPay model.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        BeamCash is not separate from SkanPay. It makes the QR checkout idea visible so merchants, banks, and payment partners can evaluate the flow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section app-flow-section" id="walkthrough">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div>
          <span>How it works</span>
          <h2>Four steps from QR request to seller status.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The demo keeps the payment moment easy to inspect. Each screen has one job.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="demo-steps" aria-label="BeamCash checkout steps">
        {beamcashFlow.map((step, index) => (
          <article>
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <strong>{step}</strong>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="app-flow-row">
        <article>
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-app-seller-dashboard.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard screen" />
          <span>Seller view</span>
          <h3>Prepare the request</h3>
          <p>The seller starts from a simple dashboard and opens the payment code.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-app-seller-code.png" alt="BeamCash seller Scan to Pay QR code screen" />
          <span>QR view</span>
          <h3>Show the Scan to Pay code</h3>
          <p>The QR screen is focused on the code, seller identity, and request state.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-app-buyer-checkout.png" alt="BeamCash buyer checkout screen" />
          <span>Buyer view</span>
          <h3>Review seller and amount</h3>
          <p>The buyer sees who they are paying and the amount before continuing.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section placement-section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div>
          <span>Use cases</span>
          <h2>Built around quick, in-person payment moments.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>BeamCash is useful as a demo because the same flow can be evaluated across real seller contexts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="placement-grid">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Pop-up vendors</h3>
          <p>A seller can display a code at a table or counter.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Creators and performers</h3>
          <p>A code can sit on a sign, stand, or printed card.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Student fundraisers</h3>
          <p>Teams can show a payment request without complex checkout setup.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Local events</h3>
          <p>Organizers can review how buyer context and seller status should work.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section demo-use-section">
    <div class="section-inner demo-use-inner">
      <div class="demo-use-copy">
        <span>What we are validating</span>
        <h2>The demo keeps product conversations concrete.</h2>
        <p>BeamCash helps separate what the seller sees, what the buyer trusts, and where partner systems fit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="use-list">
        <div>
          <strong>Seller signals</strong>
          <p>What must the seller know before and after a buyer scans?</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Buyer trust</strong>
          <p>Is the merchant, amount, and approval action clear enough?</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Partner boundary</strong>
          <p>Where do wallet, redemption, processor, and support roles sit?</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="business-cta">
    <div class="business-cta-inner">
      <div>
        <span>Feedback</span>
        <h2>Review the BeamCash flow with us.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-group">
        <a class="button primary" href={FEEDBACK_FORM_URL}>Give feedback</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href={INTEREST_LIST_URL}>Join interest list</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href={CONTACT_URL}>Request a conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
